## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to architect multi-tenant ML systems at scale on GCP, combining real-time inference, feature management, and operational governance. It tests depth across Vertex AI Feature Store, streaming data pipelines, drift detection, and cost-conscious deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- **Vertex AI Feature Store**: Per-tenant feature groups with isolated serving endpoints
- **Dataflow**: Streaming ETL from Pub/Sub with windowing and aggregations
- **BigQuery Lineage**: Schema tracking, audit logs, and feature version history
- **Canary Deployments**: Gradual rollout with tenant-specific traffic splitting
- **Drift Detection**: Statistical monitoring for data drift and model concept drift
- **Cost-Aware Rollbacks**: Automated triggers based on latency, error rates, and compute spend
- **Automated Testing**: Integration tests, A/B validation, and synthetic traffic simulation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo drift check for rollback decision
function evaluateRollback(metrics) {
  const { predictionLatency, errorRate, driftScore, costDelta } = metrics;
  const thresholds = { latencyMs: 100, errorRate: 0.01, driftScore: 0.15 };

  const shouldRollback =
    predictionLatency > thresholds.latencyMs ||
    errorRate > thresholds.errorRate ||
    driftScore > thresholds.driftScore ||
    costDelta > 0.25;

  return { shouldRollback, reason: getReason(metrics, thresholds) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end thinking, covering real-time data ingestion, data validation, model training cadence, and governance with human-in-the-loop oversight.

## Key Concepts
- **Pub/Sub** for real-time event ingestion and **Dataflow** for ETL transforms and schema validation
- **Vertex AI** for managed model training with automated pipelines
- **Vertex AI Explainable AI** for model interpretability and feature attribution
- **Cloud Monitoring** with drift detection alerts to flag model degradation
- **Cloud Tasks** for orchestrating human-in-the-loop review workflows
- Cost management strategies and governance best practices

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTicket(urgencyScore) {
  if (urgencyScore >= 0.8) {
    return { route: 'human_review', queue: 'high-urgency-tasks' };
  } else if (urgencyScore >= 0.5) {
    return { route: 'auto_process', confidence: 'medium' };
  }
  return { route: 'auto_process', confidence: 'high' };
}
```

## Rough Cost Notes
- **Pub/Sub**: ~$10/month for moderate message volume
- **Dataflow**: ~$50-100/month for batch processing
- **Cloud Storage**: ~$20/month for raw ticket storage
- **Vertex AI Training**: ~$50-200/week depending on compute
- **Vertex AI Endpoint**: ~$1-3/hour for prediction serving
- **Cloud Tasks**: ~$0.50 per 100K tasks

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect end-to-end edge ML workflows on GCP with enterprise-grade privacy, governance, and operational considerations beyond model accuracy.

## Key Concepts
- Edge model distillation and Vertex AI training pipelines
- Edge artifact distribution via Pub/Sub and Cloud CDN
- Regional canary deployments and per-tenant quotas
- Data residency, CMEK, and DLP for privacy compliance
- On-device telemetry, drift monitoring, and automated rollback

